Also in this directory in the repository, all read by the build (the app bundle carries
only this file and OFL.txt):
  anchors-400.json, anchors-700.json
      Cascadia's own dagesh anchors (the letter's anchor minus the dagesh's mark
      anchor), read from the wght 400 and 700 instances by casanchors.py.
      scripts/build-fonts.sh regenerates both on every run and stops if either differs.
      They are data read out of Cascadia Mono and are under OFL.txt beside them, as the
      font is.
  casanchors.py
      That reader.
  build/
      The build modules. build.py is the build; style.py the STYLE parameter; design.py,
      design2.py and design3.py are rounds 1-3; distinct.py is round 5 (2026-10-24),
      which moves dalet's leg so that it does not read as zayin, and round 6
      (2026-10-28), which narrows zayin's head from the left so that it does not
      read as dalet; cover.py draws the
      glyphs baud adds after them (2026-10-25: U+20AA NEW SHEQEL SIGN, drawn;
      U+05C6, U+05EF and U+05F0-U+05F2, made from the built letters; U+FB1D-U+FB4F,
      composites of the built letters and points, varika drawn, the rest from the
      built letters and JetBrains Mono's plus; U+0591-U+05AF, the cantillation
      marks, drawn), from no other font; meteg.py places meteg beside its vowel
      inside the cell (2026-10-26); optical.py is the
      italics' correction of rounds; narrow.py, field.py and geom.py are
      helpers; pin.py is the fontTools setting the bytes depend on; instance.py makes
      the instances. design*.py, narrow.py and field.py are byte-identical to the
      research tree's copies, and so is casanchors.py. In build.py and style.py the
      port changed only the paths, the imports and the save's repacker pin. Since the
      port, build.py also writes Cascadia's trademark notice into nameID 7 and adds a
      hebr script record to GSUB and GPOS (2026-10-08, conformance fixes; no outline,
      anchor, lookup or feature changed), since 2026-10-24 applies distinct.py's
      edit after design.py's, since 2026-10-25 appends cover.py's glyphs, and since
      2026-10-26 appends meteg.py's lookups.
      build.py's docstring lists the changes.
      geom.py gains flatten, segs and pt_seg_min, moved verbatim from the research
      tree's v4_clear.py, which imported uharfbuzz, so that the build imports no
      HarfBuzz. pin.py and instance.py are new.

